{"duration_api_ms":12362,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"48f65367-f04d-4248-832f-1efb7a6ccbbc","total_cost_usd":0.0015045,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2193,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1766},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2193,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1251,"outputTokens":2476,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":707,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0015045,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2026,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":707,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Rule 6c-11** (effective 2024) lets transparent index-based and actively managed ETFs operate without individual exemptive orders, if they meet daily-disclosure, basket-policy, and creation/redemption conditions. Generally covered:\n- Index-based and actively managed funds with 1x exposure, including many futures-based funds.\n\nGenerally need separate relief (outside 6c-11):\n- **Leveraged and inverse ETFs**: excluded from the rule, so they continue under individual exemptive orders.\n- **Share-class ETFs** (mutual fund share classes) and **UIT-structured ETFs**: require orders.\n- **Non-transparent active ETFs**: 6c-11 requires daily holdings disclosure, so they require orders.\n\n**Rule 18f-4** applies separately and is not waived by 6c-11. Derivatives users, including leveraged/inverse and many futures-based funds, must maintain a derivatives risk management program, meet VaR limits, and provide board oversight, unless they qualify for the limited-derivatives exception (generally 10% notional). Leveraged/inverse funds must therefore satisfy 18f-4 alongside their exemptive orders.\n\nVerify current status against the latest SEC exemptive orders and staff guidance, as this area changes.","ttft_ms":9339,"type":"result","duration_ms":11009,"uuid":"1e843c5f-d1ab-4d6d-8eeb-c4b926e04416","ttft_stream_ms":428,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":428,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
